#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2e` `the enactment as extended or applied under another provision of the same Law` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2f` `the enactment as extended or applied under another provision of the same Law` FALSE

-- "revised or otherwise consolidated" is in the text only from 28 September 2021 (V2a): V1 is silent, and the function says so.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V1` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 9(3) as it read before 28 September 2021 says amended from time to time and does not say revised or otherwise consolidated"

#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2a` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2b` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2c` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2d` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2e` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2f` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` FALSE

-- "Unless the context otherwise requires": the Article does not say what the reference is then to.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V1` `the enactment as amended` TRUE
        BECAUSE "the context otherwise requires: Article 9(3) does not say what the reference is then to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V2f` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` TRUE
        BECAUSE "the context otherwise requires: Article 9(3) does not say what the reference is then to"
-- The context clause is read before the version difference.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text V1` `the enactment as revised or otherwise consolidated` TRUE
        BECAUSE "the context otherwise requires: Article 9(3) does not say what the reference is then to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 9(3): a reference to an enactment is a reference to it in the form` `text inferred` `the enactment as amended` FALSE
        BECAUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

§ `Article 9(6): a subordinate enactment is one passed or made under a Law or under the authority of an Order in Council`

#ASSERT `Article 9(6): the instrument is a subordinate enactment` `regulations under the authority of an Order in Council`
#ASSERT `Article 9(6): the instrument is a subordinate enactment` `regulations under a Law`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(6): the instrument is a subordinate enactment` `a Law`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 9(6): the instrument is a subordinate enactment` `something that is none of these`

