§ `Article 10: expressions in an enactment passed after the commencement of the Law have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power`

-- The Law commenced on 21 August 1954.  The other enactment passed on 22 August 1954 is after it; on 20 August 1954 is before it; on 21 August 1954 the Law gives no time of day, so the Article cannot say.

#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2a` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2b` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2c` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2d` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2e` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
#ASSERT `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2f` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 22) FALSE
-- Corrected after the independent pass (NOTES 10.3, row M20): the seven on 20 August 1954 asserted FALSE; the Article does not say about an enactment passed before the commencement, so they refuse; two earlier days are added.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2a` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2b` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2c` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2d` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2e` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2f` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 20) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V1` TRUE (YMD 1954 8 19) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Article 10: the expressions used in the other enactment have the same meanings as in the enactment conferring the power` `text V2f` TRUE (YMD 1900 1 1) FALSE
        BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the same meanings only to expressions used in another enactment passed after the commencement of the Law on 21 August 1954; it does not say whether the expressions of an enactment passed before that day bear the same meanings"
